                <pb facs="0675" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.3 B 1/92: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-09-03T12:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 3,
                                1922—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 3—10:07
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>74. League has received Department’s communication of July 28th regarding
                    decision of the United States not to be a party to Arms Traffic Conference [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Convention</hi>] of Saint Germain. Commission on
                    Armaments has decided that our decision constitutes <hi rendition="#italic">fait
                        nouveau</hi> and that whole question will have to be reconsidered.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
